The <volume> of the <parallelepiped> is the <absolute value> of the <scalar triple product>:
$$
V=|\mathbf a\cdot(\mathbf b\times\mathbf c)|
=|(1,0,0)\cdot(1,0,0)|=\boxed{1}.
$$

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Equating <vector components> gives
$$
(\alpha,\beta+\gamma,\gamma)^T=(0,0,0)^T.
$$
The third component first forces $\gamma=0$, then the second forces $\beta=0$, and the first gives $\alpha=0$. Thus
$$
\boxed{\alpha=\beta=\gamma=0}.
$$
Equivalently, the nonzero <scalar triple product> proves that these three <vectors> are <linearly independent>.

