<Mutually exclusive events> have empty <intersection>. Therefore
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P(A\cap B)=0}.
$$

= b
{parent=6}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The addition formula for <probability> subtracts the overlap, which vanishes for <mutually exclusive events>:
$$
\mathbb P(A\cup B)=\mathbb P(A)+\mathbb P(B)-\mathbb P(A\cap B)
=\boxed{\mathbb P(A)+\mathbb P(B)}.
$$

= 7
{parent=Paper 2}
